{"id":"mahabharata-6-063","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":63,"title":"त्रिषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 63 · The greatness of Vasudeva","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana asks Bhishma about Vasudeva's origin and nature. Bhishma describes him as the creator and supporter of all beings and says those who take refuge in Krishna are never confused.","kn":"ವಾಸುದೇವನ ಉಗಮ ಮತ್ತು ಸ್ವರೂಪದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಭೀಷ್ಮನು ಅವನನ್ನು ಸಕಲ ಭೂತಗಳ ಸೃಷ್ಟಿಕರ್ತ, ಆಧಾರನೆಂದು ವರ್ಣಿಸಿ ಕೃಷ್ಣನ ಶರಣು ಹೋದವರಿಗೆ ಮೋಹವಿಲ್ಲವೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"दुर्योधन भीष्म से वासुदेव की उत्पत्ति और स्वरूप के बारे में पूछता है। भीष्म उन्हें सब प्राणियों का रचयिता और आधार बताते हैं और कहते हैं कि कृष्ण की शरण लेने वाले मोहित नहीं होते।","te":"వాసుదేవుని ఆవిర్భావం, స్వరూపం గురించి దుర్యోధనుడు భీష్ముని అడుగుతాడు. భీష్ముడు ఆయనను సర్వభూతాల సృష్టికర్తగా, ఆధారంగా వర్ణించి, కృష్ణుని శరణు పొందినవారు మోహపడరని అంటాడు.","ta":"வாசுதேவனின் தோற்றம், இயல்பு பற்றித் துரியோதனன் பீஷ்மரைக் கேட்கிறான். பீஷ்மர் அவரை அனைத்து உயிர்களையும் படைத்துத் தாங்குபவர் என்று விவரித்து, கண்ணனைச் சரணடைந்தோர் மயங்குவதில்லை என்கிறார்.","ml":"വാസുദേവന്റെ ഉത്ഭവത്തെയും സ്വഭാവത്തെയും കുറിച്ച് ദുര്യോധനൻ ഭീഷ്മരോട് ചോദിക്കുന്നു. സർവ ജീവജാലങ്ങളുടെയും സൃഷ്ടാവും പരിപാലകനുമായി ഭീഷ്മർ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ വർണിക്കുന്നു; കൃഷ്ണനിൽ അഭയം തേടുന്നവർ ഒരിക്കലും വഴിതെറ്റില്ലെന്ന് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.63; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"वासुदेवो महद्भूतं सर्वलोकेषु कथ्यते ।\nतस्यागमं प्रतिष्ठां च ज्ञातुमिच्छे पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva is said to be a great being in all the worlds. Grandsire, I want to know his coming and his foundation."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"वासुदेवो महद्भूतं संभूतं सह दैवतैः ।\nन परं पुण्डरीकाक्षाद्दृश्यते भरतर्षभ ।\nमार्कण्डेयश्च गोविन्दं कथयत्यद्भुतं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva is the great being, born together with the gods. Nothing higher than the lotus-eyed one is seen, bull of the Bharatas. And Markandeya tells of Govinda as a great wonder."}},{"n":3,"text":"सर्वभूतानि भूतात्मा महात्मा पुरुषोत्तमः ।\nआपो वायुश्च तेजश्च त्रयमेतदकल्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The supreme person, great self, self of all beings, devised the three, water, air and fire, for all beings."}},{"n":4,"text":"स सृष्ट्वा पृथिवीं देवः सर्वलोकेश्वरः प्रभुः ।\nअप्सु वै शयनं चक्रे महात्मा पुरुषोत्तमः ।\nसर्वतोयमयो देवो योगात्सुष्वाप तत्र ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having created the earth, the god, Lord of all worlds, the great supreme person, made his bed in the waters. Made wholly of water, the god slept there by yoga."}},{"n":5,"text":"मुखतः सोऽग्निमसृजत्प्राणाद्वायुमथापि च ।\nसरस्वतीं च वेदांश्च मनसः ससृजेऽच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From his mouth he created fire, and then wind from his breath; Sarasvati and the Vedas he created from his mind, the Unfailing One."}},{"n":6,"text":"एष लोकान्ससर्जादौ देवांश्चर्षिगणैः सह ।\nनिधनं चैव मृत्युं च प्रजानां प्रभवोऽव्ययः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He created in the beginning the worlds, and the gods with the hosts of sages; and he, the imperishable source of beings, created their death and dying."}},{"n":7,"text":"एष धर्मश्च धर्मज्ञो वरदः सर्वकामदः ।\nएष कर्ता च कार्यं च पूर्वदेवः स्वयंप्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is dharma, knower of dharma, giver of boons, giver of all desires; he is doer and deed, the first god, self-ruling."}},{"n":8,"text":"भूतं भव्यं भविष्यच्च पूर्वमेतदकल्पयत् ।\nउभे संध्ये दिशः खं च नियमं च जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He devised beforehand the past, present and future, both twilights, the directions, the sky and discipline, Janardana."}},{"n":9,"text":"ऋषींश्चैव हि गोविन्दस्तपश्चैवानु कल्पयत् ।\nस्रष्टारं जगतश्चापि महात्मा प्रभुरव्ययः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Govinda also fashioned the sages and austerity, the great imperishable lord, and the creator of the world as well."}},{"n":10,"text":"अग्रजं सर्वभूतानां संकर्षणमकल्पयत् ।\nशेषं चाकल्पयद्देवमनन्तमिति यं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He created Sankarshana, the first-born of all beings, and Shesha, the god whom they know as Ananta."}},{"n":11,"text":"यो धारयति भूतानि धरां चेमां सपर्वताम् ।\nध्यानयोगेन विप्राश्च तं वदन्ति महौजसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins call him of great energy who upholds beings and this earth with its mountains by his meditation."}},{"n":12,"text":"कर्णस्रोतोद्भवं चापि मधुं नाम महासुरम् ।\nतमुग्रमुग्रकर्माणमुग्रां बुद्धिं समास्थितम् ।\nब्रह्मणोऽपचितिं कुर्वञ्जघान पुरुषोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great asura named Madhu, who sprang from his ear, fierce, of fierce deeds and fierce mind, the supreme person killed, to do honor to Brahma."}},{"n":13,"text":"तस्य तात वधादेव देवदानवमानवाः ।\nमधुसूदनमित्याहुरृषयश्च जनार्दनम् ।\nवराहश्चैव सिंहश्च त्रिविक्रमगतिः प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that killing, my dear, gods, danavas, humans and sages call Janardana \"Madhusudana.\" He is the Boar, the Man-lion, and the Lord of the three strides."}},{"n":14,"text":"एष माता पिता चैव सर्वेषां प्राणिनां हरिः ।\nपरं हि पुण्डरीकाक्षान्न भूतं न भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"This Hari is mother and father of all creatures. There is nothing higher than the lotus-eyed, nor will there be."}},{"n":15,"text":"मुखतोऽसृजद्ब्राह्मणान्बाहुभ्यां क्षत्रियांस्तथा ।\nवैश्यांश्चाप्यूरुतो राजञ्शूद्रान्पद्भ्यां तथैव च ।\nतपसा नियतो देवो निधानं सर्वदेहिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From his mouth he created brahmins, from his arms kshatriyas, from his thighs vaishyas, king, and from his feet shudras; the god, controlled by austerity, is the treasury of all embodied beings."}},{"n":16,"text":"ब्रह्मभूतममावास्यां पौर्णमास्यां तथैव च ।\nयोगभूतं परिचरन्केशवं महदाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who serves Keshava, who has become Brahman, on the new-moon and full-moon days, and who is yoga itself, will attain greatness."}},{"n":17,"text":"केशवः परमं तेजः सर्वलोकपितामहः ।\nएवमाहुर्हृषीकेशं मुनयो वै नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keshava is the supreme light, the grandfather of all worlds. So sages call Hrishikesha, lord of men."}},{"n":18,"text":"एवमेनं विजानीहि आचार्यं पितरं गुरुम् ।\nकृष्णो यस्य प्रसीदेत लोकास्तेनाक्षया जिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know him thus as teacher, father and guru. The one with whom Krishna is pleased wins the imperishable worlds."}},{"n":19,"text":"यश्चैवैनं भयस्थाने केशवं शरणं व्रजेत् ।\nसदा नरः पठंश्चेदं स्वस्तिमान्स सुखी भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who takes refuge in Keshava in a place of fear, and who always reads this, will be blessed and happy."}},{"n":20,"text":"ये च कृष्णं प्रपद्यन्ते ते न मुह्यन्ति मानवाः ।\nभये महति ये मग्नाः पाति नित्यं जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those men who go to Krishna for shelter are not bewildered; those sunk in great fear, Janardana always protects."}},{"n":21,"text":"एतद्युधिष्ठिरो ज्ञात्वा याथातथ्येन भारत ।\nसर्वात्मना महात्मानं केशवं जगदीश्वरम् ।\nप्रपन्नः शरणं राजन्योगानामीश्वरं प्रभुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing this truly, Bharata, Yudhishthira has taken refuge with his whole self in the great-souled Keshava, Lord of the world, lord of yogas, king."}}]}]}